    "created_at": "2020-08-14T00:51:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-14T00:51:04Z",
    "body": "I'm wondering if the correct action here is to just distribute the MUSL build by default. This is e.g. [what ripgrep does](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/releases/tag/12.1.1) (they don't even offer a linux-gnu build on x86). \r\n\r\nI've also never heard of anyone downloading the MUSL build and then complaining about breakage (though granted most people probably aren't downloading the MUSL build first, so that's not a great argument about relative frequencies of breakage for MUSL/GNU).",
